INSERT INTO `quest_description_conditional` (`QuestId`, `PlayerConditionId`, `QuestgiverCreatureId`, `locale`, `Text`, `OrderIndex`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(98388, 0, 271885, 'enUS', 'Past dis bulwark, there\'s nothin but snakes, spirits, and venomous death.\n\nWe\'ve lost three lieutenants dis week. Strong ones. Brave ones. Maybe stronger and braver than you.\n\n<Mok\'sa the Stone looks you over with a weary eye.>\n\nIf you want to fling yaself into de abyss, be my guest. Bring back de scouts, if you can find dem amongst de bones.\n\nBut watch your step. Dat venom will swallow you whole.', 0, 69497), -- Into the Vaults of Atal'Utek
(98172, 160463, 270645, 'enUS', 'We must not lose sight of our true goal here in Silvermoon, $n: to bring Xal\'atath to justice.\n\nThe Void still threatens us. Their whispers emanate from every shadowed crevice within these lands. Hunt these whispers down, and silence them.', 0, 69497), -- Trailing Xal'atath
(97031, 122541, 0, 'enUS', '< A brief glint sparkling in the shadows catches your eye.\n\nAs you pick up the dust-coated hologem, the center crystal flickers briefly, revealing the words:\n\nA final memoriam.\n\nFor a moment, you see a flickering recorded projection of a male draenei speaking unheard words before the hologem fades.\n\nIt appears to be low on power.\n\nY\'mera will definitely be interested in this.>', 0, 69497), -- Vilaldoun Valediction
(96720, 158349, 265303, 'enUS', 'Despite our interference, it seems the Hal\'hadar continue their work.\n\nTheir manaforges churning all that arcane energy, their technomancers plundering the riches Naigtal has to offer.\n\nIf you can disrupt their operations and sow chaos among their forces, you will buy your precious world a moment of reprieve.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal
(96720, 158350, 265303, 'enUS', 'What a curious bog world this is!\n\nThe stench of forges indicates this world is being plundered for the riches and resources it has to offer.\n\nThe element of surprise is still in our favor. Disrupting the operations here will earn your precious world a respite.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal
(96718, 158349, 0, 'enUS', 'Despite our interference, it seems the Hal\'hadar continue their work.\n\nTheir manaforges churning all that arcane energy, their technomancers plundering the riches Naigtal has to offer.\n\nIf you can disrupt their operations and sow chaos among their forces, you will buy your precious world a moment of reprieve.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal (Heroic)
(96718, 158350, 265303, 'enUS', 'What a curious bog world this is!\n\nThe stench of forges indicates this world is being plundered for the riches and resources it has to offer.\n\nThe element of surprise is still in our favor. Disrupting the operations here will earn your precious world a respite.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal (Heroic)
(96717, 158349, 265303, 'enUS', 'Despite our interference, it seems the Hal\'hadar continue their work.\n\nTheir manaforges churning all that arcane energy, their technomancers plundering the riches Naigtal has to offer.\n\nIf you can disrupt their operations and sow chaos among their forces, you will buy your precious world a moment of reprieve.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal
(96717, 158350, 265303, 'enUS', 'What a curious bog world this is!\n\nThe stench of forges indicates this world is being plundered for the riches and resources it has to offer.\n\nThe element of surprise is still in our favor. Disrupting the operations here will earn your precious world a respite.\n\nDo what you do best, my little monster.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Naigtal
(96716, 158247, 263482, 'enUS', 'Our enemies are not yet aware of our arrival, which gives us an advantage.\n\nBy neutralizing their presence here, we buy our people back home the respite they need.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and sow chaos, champion.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Val
(96716, 158248, 263482, 'enUS', 'Despite our victories on Val, our enemy continues to mobilize their forces.\n\nWe must not let them regain the ground they have lost.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and wreak havoc across their strongholds.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Val
(96714, 158247, 263482, 'enUS', 'Our enemies are not yet aware of our arrival, which gives us an advantage.\n\nBy neutralizing their presence here, we buy our people back home the respite they need.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and sow chaos, champion.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Val (Heroic)
(96714, 158248, 263482, 'enUS', 'Despite our victories on Val, our enemy continues to mobilize their forces.\n\nWe must not let them regain the ground they have lost.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and wreak havoc across their strongholds.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Val (Heroic)
(96713, 158247, 263482, 'enUS', 'Our enemies are not yet aware of our arrival, which gives us an advantage.\n\nBy neutralizing their presence here, we buy our people back home the respite they need.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and sow chaos, champion.', 1, 69497), -- Showdown on Val
(96713, 158248, 263482, 'enUS', 'Despite our victories on Val, our enemy continues to mobilize their forces.\n\nWe must not let them regain the ground they have lost.\n\nVenture out into the frozen landscape and wreak havoc across their strongholds.', 0, 69497), -- Showdown on Val
(96703, 157437, 263479, 'enUS', 'When the Hal\'hadar attacked, we learned about their past conflicts with your fellow Lightforged.\n\nSince then, Commander Tala\'saan has been providing us information on these ethereals. His soldiers stand ready to join our cause.\n\nI\'ve requested their expertise in establishing a forward camp for our mission.\n\nAid your kin in their preparations and inform Tala\'saan we mobilize soon.', 2, 69497), -- Veterans of the Great Dark
(96703, 157436, 263479, 'enUS', 'Without your discovery of the battery core, we never would have learned about the history between your people and the Hal\'hadar.\n\nYour commander has provided information on the ethereals and sworn ground support for our mission.\n\nWe were even promised Y\'mera\'s expertise in establishing a forward camp once we touch down.\n\nAid your kin in their preparations and inform the commander we mobilize soon.', 1, 69497), -- Veterans of the Great Dark
(96703, 157076, 263479, 'enUS', 'Your recovery of the Hal\'hadar battery core revealed an unexpected ally for our operation.\n\nThe Army of the Light and these ethereals have a violent history, apparently.\n\nIn addition to the information and ground support they\'ve offered, I\'ve been promised their expertise in establishing a base camp.\n\nAid them in their preparations and inform the commander we mobilize soon.', 0, 69497), -- Veterans of the Great Dark
(96577, 5793, 0, 'enUS', 'The architect leading their operation has found a single vigilant with an intact construct core.\n\nThe other vigilants in this chamber appear to be depleted.\n\nIf she succeeds in creating a functioning Soul Lattice, the Hal\'hadar will possess the means to wield our warframes.\n\nI will disarm the waygate to prevent their escape.\n\nYou take out the architect and recover the Soul Lattice.', 0, 69497), -- The Soul Architect
(96223, 5793, 0, 'enUS', 'Champion--\n\nGrand Magister Rommath has requested your assistance. \n\nYou will find him over in the Thalassian University.', 0, 69497), -- The Magisters' Call
(96049, 157433, 263479, 'enUS', 'The keystone you found revealed much about the enemies leading these void assaults.\n\nBoth Pertinax and Leth\'ir appear to be operating from Legion worlds, which makes you a convenient expert in such terrain.\n\nI\'ve requested Belath\'s aid in navigating these worlds and fortifying our defenses.\n\nThey await you in Murder Row. Help them prepare for the assault and rally them to mobilize.', 2, 69497), -- Stalkers of the Stars
(96049, 157432, 263479, 'enUS', 'With the help of Belath Dawnblade and Decimus, we\'ve learned our enemies launch their attacks from former Legion worlds.\n\nThis makes you and your Illidari experts in such terrain.\n\nI\'ve requested your demon hunter\'s aid in navigating these worlds and fortifying our defenses.\n\nThey await you in Murder Row. Help them prepare for the assault and rally them to mobilize.', 1, 69497), -- Stalkers of the Stars
(96049, 157076, 263479, 'enUS', 'It seems both domanaar and Hal\'hadar forces are staging their attacks from former Legion worlds.\n\nIndependently, thankfully.\n\nUsing that keystone you found, Belath and Decimus have helped my Riftwalkers isolate their locations.\n\nI\'ve requested the demon hunter\'s aid in navigating these worlds and fortifying our defenses.\n\nSeek them out in Murder Row and lend them any assistance they need. Inform Belath we mobilize soon.', 0, 69497), -- Stalkers of the Stars
(95768, 0, 262669, 'enUS', 'Hey, $n.\n\nThought I might try selling some local goods here for these trolls to buy. Show \'em some real quality!\n\nI could use a break, though. Could ye watch the shop for me? If anyone comes by, just offer \'em what ye think is best.', 0, 69497), -- My Stuff's Better Than Your Stuff
(95520, 0, 267635, 'enUS', 'All dis evil flows out of de Temple of Ula\'tek. No matter how many snakes we destroy out here, dey will keep coming. And coming. Until we are overwhelmed.\n\nWarleader Abdumati and his scouts are already in there, holding back de tide. Dey could use your strength.\n\nGet in there and cut them down.', 0, 69497), -- Purging the Vaults
(95071, 155328, 0, 'enUS', 'Deepest tidings, Princess.\n\nNar\'jira the Honored graciously offers you her chosen to aid your endeavors in Eversong.\n\nAccept and behold the Deeplurk\'s mastery over the powers of old.\n\nDo not shirk this offer like the Darktide who refused her aid in their foolish pursuit the Stormcursed.\n\nOnce you have what you need, return to the deeps. When the Concord of Tides is called, we must be the first to answer.>', 0, 69497), -- Enchanted Naga Scroll
(94920, 67878, 0, 'enUS', '<The Hal\'hadar battery core has been damaged, exposing its inner workings.\n\nAmidst the thin energy wires and familiar Ka\'reshi metalwork, the gleam of argunite crystals catches your eye. Inscribed in draenic runes, you read:\n\n\"Warframe Stabilization Matrix\"\n\nYou\'ve heard rumors of ethereals spotted in the Voidstorm. Perhaps someone there could help identify what this is and who these ethereals are.>', 0, 69497), -- Hal'hadar Battery Core
(93907, 149017, 256697, 'enUS', 'When you acquire a new Seeker kit, it always starts off relatively lean. \n\nThis is because we don\'t want to overwhelm players with a multitude of rules all at once, so we allow you to get accustomed to things at your own pace.\n\nYou earn Illusionary Coins as you play. Once you\'ve amassed enough, you may trade them in with Gamemaster Fleurian for additional kits and expanded abilities on kits to which you already have access.\n\nTake the coins you earn and demonstrate your shopping prowess.', 0, 69497), -- Edification of the Worthy
(93418, 162137, 259319, 'enUS', 'I saw things in de venom haze.\n\nHeard Zul\'jan screamin\', felt what\'s eatin\' away at him. \n\nHeard Malacrass whisperin\' in his ear.\n\nUla\'tek has haunted de Amani from de beginning. De lengths we went to for power and empire, and de blood it cost...\n\nDat wasn\'t greatness. Deep down, Zul\'jan knows it too.\n\nMalacrass stole my grandfather from me. I won\'t let him take Zul\'jan too.\n\n|cffff1919<Story Mode available soon.>|r', 0, 69497), -- The Venomous Abyss
(92185, 9484, 252484, 'enUS', 'This is the time of year to reflect on the past and share stories by the fireside.\n\nOne of the most important stories is the defeat of the Frost Lord...\n\nIn summers past, in these very caverns, brave heroes joined the Earthen Ring in defeating the Frost Lord.\n\nPlace your hand upon the Ice Stone and witness this tale for yourself.', 0, 69497), -- The Tale of the Frost Lord
(88710, 140248, 245061, 'enUS', 'Champion... friend... this is it. \n\nWe must wrest the Darkwell from L\'ura, or fall to the Void. We do not have the forces available for a second chance. \n\nStrike hard, and strike true. Watch your allies\' flanks, and we will see this day won.\n\n|cffff1919<Story Mode available next week.>|r', 0, 69497), -- March on Quel'Danas
(88709, 146502, 239810, 'enUS', 'At long last, we will ride to glory and dispense justice upon this vile creature who would levy the very Void itself against us. \n\nToday is the day Xal\'atath\'s forces will face our judgement.\n\nNow is the hour we strike back!\n\nCome, let us make an end of this enemy.\n\n|cffff1919<Story Mode available next week.>|r', 0, 69497), -- The Voidspire
(77900, 146169, 0, 'enUS', 'When de loa bless the sacred rush\'kah, de masks we have made, de trials will begin. Loa be giving tasks to teach us. Once de trials start, dey don\'t stop for nobody!\n\nLet\'s go to de altar together. Witch Doctor Tzadah will lead us in de ritual. She be Master Gadrin\'s apprentice, but be showin\' real initiative in helping out on the trial.', 0, 69497), -- The Loa Trials
(49965, 146169, 0, 'enUS', 'Zul began a coup, but he did not secure de pyramid for himself. Nor has he done anything to rally more to his banner outside of those who were already conspiring with him.\n\nDis concerns me more than if he had carved his face into Dazar\'alor itself.\n\nWe must learn what he is up to. Join de disciples of Gonk and ride ahead to de Temple of the Prophet. Wardruid Loti will give you a ride. Look to her for further orders when you arrive.', 0, 69497), -- The Warpack
(27704, 146169, 0, 'enUS', 'I am Lord Itharius of the green dragonflight.\n\nThe trolls that lurk within this temple have done grievous harm to my kind, $n. We were sent here to guard this place, and were instead used to unleash the terrible powers within.$B$BI must beg you for the help only a mortal can give. You can be my hand within the temple--should I enter by myself, I risk being turned against my brothers as well.$B$BYou can start by descending the stairs behind me. Then, swim through the flooded depths of the Broken Hall. Once there, follow the passageway to the right to find the Hall of Masks.$B$BBeware of any temple guards. Once you have found the Hall of Masks, I will contact you.', 0, 69497), -- Legends of the Sunken Temple
(12721, 146169, 0, 'enUS', '$n, there is no time left. You must take this key and use it to unlock Akali.$B$BHe is being held in the courtyard in front of Gundrak, the capital of Zul\'Drak. Akali\'s chains are secured by four anchor points. You must unlock each of them to set the rhino god free.$B$BGundrak is teeming with ice trolls. However, I believe that if you\'re careful, you should be able to slip in without too much danger.$B$BOnce you\'re done, please inform the witch doctor.', 0, 69497), -- Rampage
(12628, 146169, 0, 'enUS', 'The gods have spoken to me, $n. I know what you must do.$B$BYou must go to the Altar of Har\'koa to the southeast and speak with the leopard goddess.', 0, 69497); -- To Speak With Har'koa
